WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.386
Alpha-gal companion.

2
00:00:02.336 --> 00:00:11.480
Tick-Primed Hypersensitivity in Cosmetic and Aesthetic Procedures, by Marielle He, Jordan Kai Simmons, and Babak Azizzadeh.

3
00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:16.480
This is the digital companion: Screen, Stratify, Act.

4
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.728
Sensitized does not equal reactive.

5
00:00:19.728 --> 00:00:32.173
Alpha-gal syndrome, or A-G-S, requires a compatible history plus alpha-gal–specific I-G-E. Confirmation defines the diagnosis; it is not a per-procedure laboratory gate.

6
00:00:32.173 --> 00:00:36.535
Entry question, all patients: compatible history?

7
00:00:36.535 --> 00:00:48.940
Delayed urticaria, gastrointestinal symptoms, or anaphylaxis three to six hours after mammalian meat; tick exposure; or residence in an endemic lone-star tick region.

8
00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:52.744
Tier 1, low: no suggestive history.

9
00:00:52.744 --> 00:00:59.524
Do not screen alpha-gal specific I-G-E and do not restrict materials on an A-G-S basis.

10
00:00:59.524 --> 00:01:04.551
Endemic residence alone, without symptoms, remains Tier 1.

11
00:01:04.551 --> 00:01:07.092
Proceed with standard care.

12
00:01:07.092 --> 00:01:13.437
Tier 2, caution: suspected A-G-S. Order alpha-gal specific I-G-E.

13
00:01:13.437 --> 00:01:22.269
A value of 0.1 kilounits per liter is detectable; conventional positivity is commonly 0.35.

14
00:01:22.269 --> 00:01:24.714
Interpret with the history.

15
00:01:24.714 --> 00:01:27.826
Refer to allergy and immunology.

16
00:01:27.826 --> 00:01:31.684
Prefer non-mammalian materials pending results.

17
00:01:31.684 --> 00:01:35.529
If the procedure is urgent, manage as Tier 3.

18
00:01:35.529 --> 00:01:42.499
Tier 3, act: established A-G-S. Default to source-verified non-mammalian substitutes.

19
00:01:42.499 --> 00:01:44.646
Involve allergy.

20
00:01:44.646 --> 00:01:48.967
Anaphylaxis plan with epinephrine immediately available.

21
00:01:48.967 --> 00:01:54.456
Not an absolute contraindication if no non-mammalian option exists.

22
00:01:54.456 --> 00:01:58.532
Identify every mammalian-derived item on the field.

23
00:01:58.532 --> 00:02:06.888
Verify species, source, excipients, and lot against the current instructions for use, not the brand name alone.

24
00:02:06.888 --> 00:02:11.711
Substitute when a source-verified non-mammalian option exists.

25
00:02:11.711 --> 00:02:17.608
If none exists, flag for allergy input and anaphylaxis precautions.

26
00:02:17.608 --> 00:02:21.426
Oral exposure is delayed three to six hours.

27
00:02:21.426 --> 00:02:24.524
Parenteral exposure may be immediate.

28
00:02:24.524 --> 00:02:27.391
Implants can prolong exposure.

29
00:02:27.391 --> 00:02:31.603
Food-challenge thresholds do not establish product safety.

30
00:02:31.603 --> 00:02:38.614
The established pathway is tick-induced alpha-gal I-G-E reacting to a later mammalian exposure.

31
00:02:38.614 --> 00:02:44.524
A hypothesized product-associated sensitization pathway remains unestablished.

32
00:02:44.524 --> 00:02:49.239
Material risk, evidence strength separate from clinical action.

33
00:02:49.239 --> 00:02:54.470
Demonstrated: gelatin hemostats — avoid; use non-gelatin.

34
00:02:54.470 --> 00:03:18.002
Clinical signal: porcine unfractionated heparin — 4 of 17 severe reactions, or 24 percent, with high-dose intravenous cardiac exposure; 4 of 8 with recent titers, or 50 percent; lower-dose inpatient unfractionated heparin, 1 of 39, or 2.6 percent; enoxaparin, 0 of 22.

35
00:03:18.002 --> 00:03:20.421
Substitute if feasible.

36
00:03:20.421 --> 00:03:27.432
Mechanistic inference: mammalian matrices; no prospective cosmetic or aesthetic cohort.

37
00:03:27.432 --> 00:03:31.589
Theoretical: collagen P-M-M-A and catgut.

38
00:03:31.589 --> 00:03:40.353
Testicular hyaluronidase is theoretical for alpha-gal only; a separate non-A-G-S anaphylaxis risk is label-documented.

39
00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:43.260
Prefer recombinant Hylenex.

40
00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:46.997
Theoretical does not equal low overall risk.

41
00:03:46.997 --> 00:04:01.752
No A-G-S-specific risk identified in the available literature for source-verified hyaluronic acid, calcium hydroxylapatite, poly-L-lactic acid, lidocaine, and botulinum toxin after label check.

42
00:04:01.752 --> 00:04:04.252
That is not proven safe.

43
00:04:04.252 --> 00:04:11.535
Delayed filler or matrix reactions do not prove A-G-S, and alpha-gal screening will not detect them.

44
00:04:11.535 --> 00:04:22.826
No prospective cosmetic or aesthetic cohort, validated procedure-specific screening threshold, reaction registry, or brand-level alpha-gal assay exists.

45
00:04:22.826 --> 00:04:28.315
Version 2.0, reviewed 28 August 2026.

46
00:04:28.315 --> 00:04:30.434
Disclosures none.

47
00:04:30.434 --> 00:04:32.296
Funding none.

48
00:04:32.296 --> 00:04:39.660
The optional questionnaire is an internal feasibility inspection copy; responses are not collected here.

49
00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:45.774
This narration is decision support for licensed clinicians, not medical advice.

50
00:04:45.774 --> 00:04:50.149
Premedication does not reliably prevent anaphylaxis.

51
00:04:50.149 --> 00:04:52.173
End of narration.
